      <header class="worship-intro"><p class="eyebrow">A serious note</p><p class="worship-constellation" aria-hidden="true">✦&nbsp;✧&nbsp;✦</p><h1>Discretion.</h1></header>
      <div class="worship-prose privacy-prose">
        <p>Short and serious, because this matters more to me than almost anything else on this site.</p>
        <p>Before I was a Goddess, I was an engineer. I still am, underneath the ink. I understand security, encryption, data, and digital footprints at a level most people claiming to value your privacy never will. This is not a promise copied from a template. It is a competence. I do not just intend to protect you. I know how to think about protection.</p>
        <h2>What that means <em>practically.</em></h2>
        <p>Your information is handled like the asset it is. Your intake, tributes, and messages are not published or placed in a public-facing site database. For now, intake answers are delivered to Emilia for review, and the site does not retain a copy after sending them. The private CRM now in development will move intake storage to encrypted, on-server storage under Emilia’s control. I think about data the way an engineer thinks about data: what is stored, where, who could reach it, and how to reduce that answer.</p>
        <p>My own security is professional-minded, and yours inherits that care. Dedicated accounts, clear boundaries, and separate personal and creator infrastructure mean that I keep my life compartmentalized. If you are the kind of person who thinks about these things, you will find comfort in how much thought I put into them.</p>
        <p>What happens between us stays between us. Always. I do not share names, screenshots that identify you, or details that could connect your tribute to your life. The people in my world are doctors, executives, engineers, politicians, parents, partners, and quiet professionals of every kind, and every one of them came to me because I understand what discretion is worth structurally, not just as a courtesy.</p>
        <p>Discretion is a two-way street, and I only walk it with those who deserve my time. What you learn about me here stays here. What you see of my life stays in your memory, not in your group chats. My security practices protect me from the world; your discretion protects us from you.</p>
        <h2>A few practical notes, for the <em>careful ones.</em></h2>
        <ul class="privacy-notes">
          <li>Tribute avenues are selected with discretion in mind. Review an avenue’s terms and your own statements before you send.</li>
          <li>Your intake is for Emilia’s review alone. It is not sold, published, or used for anything except understanding how to take care of you properly. Do not include passwords, account credentials, government IDs, or anything you would not want sent by email.</li>
          <li>Photo-album access uses a server-side session. It is a privacy gate, not a substitute for a bespoke identity or CRM system.</li>
          <li>Have specific privacy needs? Tell me in your intake. An engineer does not flinch at edge cases; an engineer designs for them. Clear requirements make careful handling possible.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>You have a life. I protect it.</p>
        <p>That is part of what my generosity buys, part of what my engineering guarantees, and a very large part of why my subs stay for years. 🖤</p>
